1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:05,130
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

2
00:00:09,134 --> 00:00:10,760
♪ <i>Oh, Mister</i> ♪

3
00:00:10,844 --> 00:00:12,887
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

4
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut and it's over</i> ♪

5
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,476
- Tatoy!
- [Atoy] My child?

6
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:19,477
Ibyang!

7
00:00:19,561 --> 00:00:21,062
[Red] <i>You've cornered me already.</i>

8
00:00:21,146 --> 00:00:22,188
<i>So, we're all going down together.</i>

9
00:00:22,272 --> 00:00:23,189
I'll start with your daughter.

10
00:00:24,149 --> 00:00:24,983
Tatoy!

11
00:00:25,066 --> 00:00:27,193
[dagger swishes]

12
00:00:27,277 --> 00:00:29,362
[dramatic sting]

13
00:00:29,446 --> 00:00:31,239
[Gavin] Stay here first. Okay? I'll help.

14
00:00:31,322 --> 00:00:32,198
I don't want anything bad

15
00:00:32,282 --> 00:00:33,825
to happen to you because

16
00:00:33,908 --> 00:00:35,452
you're important to me, Gavin.

17
00:00:35,535 --> 00:00:37,037
Why are you telling me that?

18
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:39,039
- I like you, Gavin.
- Really?

19
00:00:39,122 --> 00:00:41,708
- [Paldo] <i>Where's Ibyang?</i>
- [Nestor] <i>Maybe Atoy looked for Ibyang.</i>

20
00:00:41,791 --> 00:00:43,168
Tatoy!

21
00:00:43,251 --> 00:00:45,336
[Ibyang] <i>I'll find a way!</i>

22
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:47,297
[sobs] <i>Don't let go, okay!</i>

23
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:49,507
[grunting]

24
00:00:49,591 --> 00:00:50,508
PREVIOUSLY

25
00:00:50,592 --> 00:00:53,595
[Ibyang] <i>Good thing you didn't fall.</i>

26
00:00:53,678 --> 00:00:55,805
<i>I'd really pinch your ear!</i>

27
00:00:55,889 --> 00:00:57,307
Good thing then.

28
00:00:57,390 --> 00:01:01,686
[Mercado] <i>They say it takes a village</i>
<i>to execute an operation.</i>

29
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:05,065
<i>But the truth is, it is all</i>
<i>because of one man.</i>

30
00:01:05,148 --> 00:01:06,983
[in English] <i>The Master Cutter.</i>

31
00:01:08,401 --> 00:01:09,402
[Atoy, in English] <i>Are you in position?</i>

32
00:01:09,486 --> 00:01:10,612
[in English] <i>I'm on my way.</i>

33
00:01:10,695 --> 00:01:11,571
[Audrey, in English] <i>What's going on?</i>

34
00:01:12,197 --> 00:01:13,281
[Janine] <i>Just wait.</i>

35
00:01:16,034 --> 00:01:18,828
[in English] Audrey Regalia,
will you marry me?

36
00:01:18,912 --> 00:01:20,038
[Emerson giggles]

37
00:01:20,121 --> 00:01:20,997
[in English] Yes!

38
00:01:21,081 --> 00:01:26,002
[exclaiming and cheering]

39
00:01:26,669 --> 00:01:28,671
[Ibyang] <i>The Lord is truly amazing,</i>

40
00:01:29,422 --> 00:01:32,133
<i>because He listened to my prayer.</i>

41
00:01:32,217 --> 00:01:33,176
<i>But look.</i>

42
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:36,763
<i>I have Tatoy and Mommy now.</i>

43
00:01:37,597 --> 00:01:39,098
<i>I even have a sister!</i>

44
00:01:39,182 --> 00:01:41,017
[in English] And now,
you may kiss the bride.

45
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:43,353
[elated shriek]

46
00:01:43,436 --> 00:01:46,189
[exclaiming and cheering]

47
00:01:46,272 --> 00:01:47,482
[all] One more!

48
00:01:47,565 --> 00:01:49,567
[exclaiming and cheering]

49
00:01:49,651 --> 00:01:50,610
[indistinct]

50
00:01:50,693 --> 00:01:52,112
[Mercado on phone, in English]
<i>I know you're on leave,</i>

51
00:01:52,195 --> 00:01:54,072
<i>but I just had to let you know.</i>

52
00:01:54,155 --> 00:01:55,657
<i>Samir escaped</i>

53
00:01:55,740 --> 00:01:57,200
<i>just this morning</i>

54
00:01:57,283 --> 00:01:58,451
<i>from the hospital,</i>

55
00:01:58,535 --> 00:02:00,370
<i>before he was transferred to prison.</i>

56
00:02:00,954 --> 00:02:02,163
<i>Be careful still.</i>

57
00:02:05,542 --> 00:02:06,668
[music concludes]

58
00:02:09,295 --> 00:02:10,421
Janine?

59
00:02:11,631 --> 00:02:12,465
Ibyang?

60
00:02:12,549 --> 00:02:14,300
[Janine] I'm just chasing Ibyang!

61
00:02:14,384 --> 00:02:15,510
What's with you both?

62
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:18,388
Hey, help me with grilling here!

63
00:02:18,471 --> 00:02:20,473
- [Ibyang] Later!
- Audrey!

64
00:02:20,557 --> 00:02:21,808
Audrey, come here! Quick!

65
00:02:23,518 --> 00:02:24,727
- Come!
- [gentle music playing]

66
00:02:24,811 --> 00:02:25,854
Look at it! It's beautiful!

67
00:02:27,438 --> 00:02:28,690
[in English] It's perfect!

68
00:02:29,482 --> 00:02:30,567
It's beautiful!

69
00:02:31,442 --> 00:02:32,819
Just like you!

70
00:02:34,737 --> 00:02:38,032
- Hey! Quit fooling around!
- [chuckling]

71
00:02:38,116 --> 00:02:39,909
[giggling]

72
00:02:39,993 --> 00:02:42,453
[Audrey] Janine! Ibyang!

73
00:02:42,537 --> 00:02:44,330
- Come here!
- [Janine, in English] Yes?

74
00:02:44,414 --> 00:02:45,874
Look at the sunset!

75
00:02:45,957 --> 00:02:47,167
- [in English] Look, look!
- [Audrey] Beautiful!

76
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:48,668
[Janine] Wow!

77
00:02:48,751 --> 00:02:49,961
[in English] Love you, baby.

78
00:02:53,798 --> 00:02:55,717
[Ibyang] Tatoy! Mommy!

79
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:59,345
[Ibyang] Thank you for…

80
00:02:59,971 --> 00:03:02,181
[Janine, in English] Thank you,
Mommy and Daddy.

81
00:03:02,265 --> 00:03:04,392
This is one of my favorite days.

82
00:03:07,395 --> 00:03:11,608
[intense music playing]

83
00:03:26,247 --> 00:03:27,457
[woman panting]

84
00:03:28,708 --> 00:03:30,001
[woman gasps]

85
00:03:37,175 --> 00:03:39,928
[panting, sobs]

86
00:03:45,683 --> 00:03:46,517
‪[steady breathing]

87
00:03:55,902 --> 00:04:00,198
[intense music playing]

88
00:04:00,949 --> 00:04:01,783
‪[gasps]

89
00:04:09,332 --> 00:04:10,166
‪[steady breathing]

90
00:04:13,378 --> 00:04:14,212
‪[music intensifies]

91
00:04:21,469 --> 00:04:22,387
‪[music stops]

92
00:04:26,266 --> 00:04:27,100
‪[tense music playing]

93
00:04:27,183 --> 00:04:28,518
- Ibyang.
- <i>Tatoy?</i>

94
00:04:28,601 --> 00:04:30,770
Where are you now? Are you safe?

95
00:04:31,396 --> 00:04:33,815
<i>Yes. I'm far from the base.</i>

96
00:04:35,942 --> 00:04:37,860
<i>Janine!</i>

97
00:04:38,486 --> 00:04:39,779
<i>She separated from me.</i>

98
00:04:40,405 --> 00:04:41,906
<i>But I know where she is.</i>

99
00:04:41,990 --> 00:04:43,199
[in English] That's good!

100
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:45,326
[in English] Okay. Just stay low!

101
00:04:45,952 --> 00:04:46,786
[leaves crunch]

102
00:04:46,869 --> 00:04:47,704
Just hide.

103
00:04:47,787 --> 00:04:49,580
[in English] Just stay low! Okay?

104
00:04:51,082 --> 00:04:53,751
[gunshots blast]

105
00:04:54,919 --> 00:04:58,298
[gunshots blasting]

106
00:05:03,136 --> 00:05:06,973
[gunshots blasting]

107
00:05:07,515 --> 00:05:09,350
[gunshots blast]

108
00:05:09,434 --> 00:05:14,939
[panting]

109
00:05:16,566 --> 00:05:19,277
[music fades]

110
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:22,947
- [tense music playing]
- [gasps]

111
00:05:23,990 --> 00:05:26,159
- Oh, where are the kids?
- [chuckles]

112
00:05:26,242 --> 00:05:27,452
Why is it just you?

113
00:05:29,329 --> 00:05:35,335
[gunshots blasting]

114
00:05:41,340 --> 00:05:42,467
[man grunts]

115
00:05:42,550 --> 00:05:44,927
- Who are you?
- I won't hurt you.

116
00:05:45,011 --> 00:05:47,430
[in English] You're good. [sighs]

117
00:05:47,513 --> 00:05:49,182
The Agency will protect you.

118
00:05:53,770 --> 00:05:57,315
THE MASTER CUTTER
CHILDREN OF THE THREAD

119
00:06:00,485 --> 00:06:02,403
- Uh… [screams]
-

120
00:06:03,112 --> 00:06:05,490
- Let's go!
- [light pleasant music playing]

121
00:06:05,573 --> 00:06:06,783
- [Atoy] Let's go, oh!
- [indistinct]

122
00:06:06,866 --> 00:06:07,784
[Atoy] Janine? Ibyang?

123
00:06:07,867 --> 00:06:09,452
- I caught your mother!
- [indistinct]

124
00:06:09,535 --> 00:06:11,454
We're going to make her into a lechon!

125
00:06:11,537 --> 00:06:13,498
[Audrey] Put me down!

126
00:06:13,581 --> 00:06:14,665
- Huh?
- Hey!

127
00:06:14,749 --> 00:06:16,542
If you turn me into a lechon,
you'll only be hungry

128
00:06:16,626 --> 00:06:18,669
because I don't have a lot of meat!

129
00:06:18,753 --> 00:06:20,421
[Ibyang] It's because you're big, Tatoy!

130
00:06:20,505 --> 00:06:23,049
That's why Mommy saw you!

131
00:06:23,132 --> 00:06:24,717
[Atoy chuckles] Okay, alright.

132
00:06:24,801 --> 00:06:27,136
I'm sorry. Alright, you go to sleep.

133
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:29,847
[Audrey] It's because we need
to wake up early tomorrow.

134
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:33,392
- Because we have a surprise for you guys!
- [girls shriek]

135
00:06:33,476 --> 00:06:34,352
[Audrey] Mmm…

136
00:06:34,435 --> 00:06:35,520
[Audrey] What is it?

137
00:06:35,603 --> 00:06:37,271
[Ibyang] Hmm. It's a surprise!

138
00:06:37,355 --> 00:06:40,358
[Ibyang] But you can also
tell us now, Tatoy.

139
00:06:40,441 --> 00:06:41,776
[Ibyang] Come on!

140
00:06:41,859 --> 00:06:46,155
[Atoy and Audrey, in English]
One, two, three, surprise!

141
00:06:46,239 --> 00:06:48,741
[gasps] It's beautiful! [giggles]

142
00:06:48,825 --> 00:06:50,326
- Uh-huh. Huh?
- [Audrey chuckles]

143
00:06:50,409 --> 00:06:52,036
[light pleasant music playing]

144
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:53,412
Are we going to live here?

145
00:06:54,330 --> 00:06:56,707
- Yes.
- [in English] Oh, I love it!

146
00:06:56,791 --> 00:06:58,709
I like it here more!

147
00:06:58,793 --> 00:07:01,170
[exclaims and giggles]

148
00:07:01,254 --> 00:07:04,298
So, do you want a house tour?

149
00:07:04,382 --> 00:07:05,216
- Come on.
- [in English] Yes.

150
00:07:05,299 --> 00:07:07,218
- Let's go to your room.
- [in English] Let's go, let's go!

151
00:07:07,301 --> 00:07:08,219
[girls shrieking]

152
00:07:08,302 --> 00:07:09,887
- Oops! Careful, it's still
- [Cita] Hey.

153
00:07:09,971 --> 00:07:11,013
dusty!

154
00:07:11,097 --> 00:07:12,515
Come in, come in.

155
00:07:12,598 --> 00:07:13,933
- [Cita] It's beautiful.
- Oh?

156
00:07:14,016 --> 00:07:15,476
- Come in, come in.
-

157
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:16,477
Over there in the kitchen.

158
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:17,728
There! It's so beautiful.

159
00:07:17,812 --> 00:07:18,980
Be careful, Brother Kurt!

160
00:07:19,689 --> 00:07:21,065
Bring that in!

161
00:07:21,149 --> 00:07:24,026
Oop, oop, oop.
Ah, ah-- 'Son, 'Son, 'Son, careful--

162
00:07:24,110 --> 00:07:25,736
- Emerson--
- [Emerson] Move it like this, quick.

163
00:07:25,820 --> 00:07:27,530
- Maybe we need to do it this way.
- No, we got this.

164
00:07:27,613 --> 00:07:28,656
- We can do this, Tatoy.
- Can you?

165
00:07:28,739 --> 00:07:30,283
- [Emerson] Move it like this, like this.
- [man] Just pull it!

166
00:07:30,366 --> 00:07:32,869
- [Cita squeals]
- [indistinct chatter]

167
00:07:32,952 --> 00:07:35,288
- [Atoy] Okay, let's help, let's help.
- [Emerson] Wait, wait.

168
00:07:35,371 --> 00:07:36,998
- Because you said move it like this.
- [overlapping chatter]

169
00:07:37,081 --> 00:07:39,250
[Emerson] Unbelievable!
How do we bring it inside?

170
00:07:39,333 --> 00:07:40,543
- It might break!
- [overlapping chatter]

171
00:07:40,626 --> 00:07:41,669
- Why are you pushing it that way?
- [woman squeals]

172
00:07:41,752 --> 00:07:42,879
- [Atoy, in English] One, two.
- [Emerson] There, okay, that's it.

173
00:07:42,962 --> 00:07:44,046
- [Emerson] No, no, no. No, no, no.
- [woman squeals]

174
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:45,423
- [Cita] Here, here. Here!
- What's really the plan? Ame

175
00:07:45,506 --> 00:07:46,549
should be lifting here, Ame!

176
00:07:46,632 --> 00:07:47,508
[Cita] Here, here, here, here!

177
00:07:47,592 --> 00:07:52,096
[clamoring]

178
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:53,598
[Emerson] It might fall! It might fall!

179
00:07:53,681 --> 00:07:54,974
[Cita] Oh, oh.

180
00:07:55,057 --> 00:07:56,058
[indistinct chattering]

181
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:58,352
- Here!
- Oop! Oop, oop, oop!

182
00:07:58,436 --> 00:08:00,354
- Oh, oh, oh!
- [indistinct chattering]

183
00:08:00,438 --> 00:08:01,397
I think it looks better
in the middle, like--

184
00:08:01,481 --> 00:08:02,356
It's very avant garde.

185
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:04,400
- Here! Here, here, here.
- [indistinct]

186
00:08:04,484 --> 00:08:06,110
- [Cita] Move it more, move it.
- [Emerson] Okay, let's go.

187
00:08:06,194 --> 00:08:07,111
- Move it, move it, move it.
- There, that's it.

188
00:08:07,195 --> 00:08:08,571
That's perfect. Then curtains--

189
00:08:08,654 --> 00:08:11,532
[lively chattering]

190
00:08:11,616 --> 00:08:12,992
- [Cita sighs]
- [Karla] Wow!

191
00:08:13,075 --> 00:08:14,827
- [Cita] I'm happy.
- [indistinct]

192
00:08:14,911 --> 00:08:16,078
[Atoy] Are you all okay there?

193
00:08:16,162 --> 00:08:18,122
- [Karla] Where's Big Sister Ame?
- [Cita] Oh, oh?

194
00:08:18,206 --> 00:08:19,540
[overlapping chatter]

195
00:08:19,624 --> 00:08:21,417
Wow!

196
00:08:22,210 --> 00:08:24,337
- [Jona] It's so beautiful!
- Congrats, Atoy!

197
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:27,673
- It's beautiful! You've leveled up!
- Right? Is it nice?

198
00:08:27,757 --> 00:08:28,799
It's golden!

199
00:08:28,883 --> 00:08:30,593
[chuckles] Hey, congrats!

200
00:08:30,676 --> 00:08:31,802
- Congrats, miss.
- [Atoy] Sir Nestor.

201
00:08:31,886 --> 00:08:32,845
- [Nestor] Let's drink here!
- [Cita] Oh!

202
00:08:32,929 --> 00:08:33,804
- It's prohibited!
- [elated shrieking]

203
00:08:33,888 --> 00:08:34,805
Prohibited, prohibited,

204
00:08:34,889 --> 00:08:36,516
prohibited, prohibited,
prohibited, prohibited.

205
00:08:36,599 --> 00:08:37,433
Miss Siony.

206
00:08:37,517 --> 00:08:38,434
[lively chatter]

207
00:08:38,518 --> 00:08:40,228
Thank you. Here's the kitchen.

208
00:08:40,311 --> 00:08:41,145
‪[Siony laughs]

209
00:08:41,729 --> 00:08:43,356
Just here. Just here.

210
00:08:43,439 --> 00:08:44,482
There, there, there.

211
00:08:44,565 --> 00:08:46,192
- [lively chattering]
- [elated gasp]

212
00:08:46,275 --> 00:08:48,319
Oh, Atoy!

213
00:08:48,402 --> 00:08:51,447
Congratulations indeed!

214
00:08:51,531 --> 00:08:55,243
Your most important and longest mission
was a success.

215
00:08:55,326 --> 00:08:57,411
To have a happy and complete family

216
00:08:57,495 --> 00:08:59,080
under one roof!

217
00:08:59,163 --> 00:09:00,873
- Yay!
- Wait.

218
00:09:00,957 --> 00:09:01,958
And there's more.

219
00:09:02,041 --> 00:09:03,209
[giggles]

220
00:09:03,292 --> 00:09:05,586
Yes, where are they?

221
00:09:05,670 --> 00:09:07,046
- Touring?
- Yes, oh my.

222
00:09:07,129 --> 00:09:09,507
- Yay!
- They're arranging the toys.

223
00:09:09,590 --> 00:09:12,009
[Audrey] Ta-da!

224
00:09:12,093 --> 00:09:13,928
Mommy, I'll sleep here, okay?

225
00:09:14,011 --> 00:09:15,471
- Psst.
- I got here first.

226
00:09:16,097 --> 00:09:20,726
While the other mattress
hasn't been delivered yet,

227
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:22,562
you'll sleep together for now.

228
00:09:22,645 --> 00:09:24,897
[light music playing]

229
00:09:24,981 --> 00:09:27,650
Janine, you can't refuse.

230
00:09:28,192 --> 00:09:29,443
What do you want?

231
00:09:29,527 --> 00:09:30,736
For me to sleep on the floor?

232
00:09:31,904 --> 00:09:33,489
Okay, that's fine.

233
00:09:33,573 --> 00:09:34,740
If you want.

234
00:09:35,283 --> 00:09:38,619
For me, it's fine. I'm good.

235
00:09:39,161 --> 00:09:41,998
Ahh. Yes.

236
00:09:42,540 --> 00:09:44,417
I'll sleep beside you,

237
00:09:45,084 --> 00:09:46,419
even if you don't want me to.

238
00:09:47,587 --> 00:09:50,214
You two, really! Hmm!

239
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:52,258
Okay then. Oh!

240
00:09:52,341 --> 00:09:54,927
So, do you like this room?

241
00:09:55,886 --> 00:09:57,597
Everything is beautiful!

242
00:09:58,389 --> 00:09:59,223
[Atoy] Is it okay?

243
00:09:59,307 --> 00:10:01,851
Mmm-mmm. Thank you for the new house.

244
00:10:01,934 --> 00:10:03,060
Of course.

245
00:10:03,144 --> 00:10:04,604
[in English] Thank you too, Daddy.

246
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:06,564
- [chuckling]
- It's beautiful.

247
00:10:06,647 --> 00:10:08,774
- Uh, Tatoy…
- [Atoy] Hmm?

248
00:10:08,858 --> 00:10:12,111
What will happen to the old house?

249
00:10:12,194 --> 00:10:13,446
It stays.

250
00:10:13,529 --> 00:10:15,906
Whatever is there, I won't change it,

251
00:10:15,990 --> 00:10:17,325
because I don't want to erase

252
00:10:17,408 --> 00:10:19,535
the memory of your Grandpa Delfin.

253
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:21,662
[Ibyang] Hm-mm.

254
00:10:21,746 --> 00:10:25,458
But what about the secret room?

255
00:10:25,541 --> 00:10:26,375
[Janine] Exactly.

256
00:10:28,169 --> 00:10:29,754
[in English] Secret room?

257
00:10:29,837 --> 00:10:31,464
[pensive music playing]

258
00:10:31,547 --> 00:10:34,842
What secret room, love?

259
00:10:35,384 --> 00:10:38,763
Uh, I've been there, Mommy.

260
00:10:38,846 --> 00:10:41,641
There are wigs there, lots of them.

261
00:10:41,724 --> 00:10:44,268
And knives and…

262
00:10:47,980 --> 00:10:49,732
Hmm…

263
00:10:49,815 --> 00:10:51,484
Why haven't you told me

264
00:10:51,567 --> 00:10:53,235
you have a secret room, love?

265
00:10:54,487 --> 00:10:55,613
[Audrey] We're married, right?

266
00:10:56,280 --> 00:10:58,407
We shouldn't have secrets.

267
00:10:58,491 --> 00:10:59,867
Well, now you know.

268
00:10:59,950 --> 00:11:01,744
[sneaky music playing]

269
00:11:01,827 --> 00:11:02,703
That's why it's a secret room,

270
00:11:02,787 --> 00:11:05,039
because no one can enter, except me.

271
00:11:05,122 --> 00:11:07,750
There are dangerous things
there that I use for--

272
00:11:07,833 --> 00:11:08,834
You know.

273
00:11:08,918 --> 00:11:11,462
But these two… These two little kids…

274
00:11:11,545 --> 00:11:12,421
[chuckles]

275
00:11:12,505 --> 00:11:13,672
They suddenly…

276
00:11:13,756 --> 00:11:14,965
Because they're so hyper,

277
00:11:15,049 --> 00:11:16,258
they snuck in when they shouldn't have.

278
00:11:18,219 --> 00:11:19,345
[Janine chuckles]

279
00:11:19,887 --> 00:11:20,846
[Atoy] So, love?

280
00:11:20,930 --> 00:11:22,681
Are you happy with our room?

281
00:11:25,267 --> 00:11:26,352
[in English] Love…

282
00:11:27,061 --> 00:11:28,354
[Atoy] Hmm?

283
00:11:28,437 --> 00:11:30,022
I wanted to talk to you.

284
00:11:31,148 --> 00:11:34,610
- Mmm.
- About your secret room.

285
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:37,947
- [in English] Okay.
- [camera shutter snaps]

286
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:43,285
Since it's still there, does that mean

287
00:11:44,870 --> 00:11:46,956
you'll continue your old job?

288
00:11:47,039 --> 00:11:48,207
Don't worry.

289
00:11:48,290 --> 00:11:52,002
I'll finish our move first
before I go back.

290
00:11:52,711 --> 00:11:55,423
Ah, I thought the reason we moved was

291
00:11:56,799 --> 00:11:59,802
so we could start again as a family?

292
00:12:00,678 --> 00:12:02,888
That you'd leave your old life behind.

293
00:12:02,972 --> 00:12:05,891
And it's been months since you
accepted a mission, right?

294
00:12:07,017 --> 00:12:10,146
Love, listen to me first.

295
00:12:10,229 --> 00:12:12,481
You can still continue the tailoring shop.

296
00:12:12,565 --> 00:12:17,111
The income just isn't as big
compared to being a tracker.

297
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:19,029
But

298
00:12:20,156 --> 00:12:21,907
I also have a job.

299
00:12:23,242 --> 00:12:25,035
We'll help each other.

300
00:12:25,119 --> 00:12:27,872
[pensive music playing]

301
00:12:27,955 --> 00:12:28,998
I know.

302
00:12:30,666 --> 00:12:33,419
I won't be a tracker forever anyway.

303
00:12:33,502 --> 00:12:35,129
But when will you stop?

304
00:12:37,089 --> 00:12:39,008
When it already affects us?

305
00:12:39,091 --> 00:12:41,552
[soft drama music playing]

306
00:12:41,635 --> 00:12:42,636
[in English] Love…

307
00:12:44,597 --> 00:12:45,764
I want us

308
00:12:47,683 --> 00:12:49,101
to have another baby.

309
00:12:53,063 --> 00:12:54,315
Me too.

310
00:12:56,484 --> 00:12:58,986
If you continue being a tracker…

311
00:13:01,614 --> 00:13:05,242
can you promise me nothing bad
will happen to you?

312
00:13:05,868 --> 00:13:08,329
You already have your own family.

313
00:13:09,038 --> 00:13:12,333
I hope you understand
why I'm asking you to quit that job.

314
00:13:28,933 --> 00:13:30,100
You know, Atoy,

315
00:13:30,184 --> 00:13:34,146
I get why you can't let go
of being a tracker.

316
00:13:35,064 --> 00:13:37,775
Of course, you're looking
for the thrill, the…

317
00:13:37,858 --> 00:13:41,862
adrenaline rush, the pew,
pew-pew, pew. Right?

318
00:13:41,946 --> 00:13:44,698
But of course, that's fine
if you're still single.

319
00:13:45,574 --> 00:13:47,326
But Atoy, you have a family now.

320
00:13:48,577 --> 00:13:50,329
And maybe you're forgetting.

321
00:13:51,205 --> 00:13:53,499
The ones you go up against
are on another level.

322
00:13:54,291 --> 00:13:55,751
You've even been captured.

323
00:13:55,834 --> 00:13:58,754
Good thing we, the Children
of the Thread, rescued you.

324
00:13:58,837 --> 00:14:01,048
What if we weren't there, huh?
What would have happened to you?

325
00:14:01,131 --> 00:14:02,132
You'd be dead.

326
00:14:02,841 --> 00:14:04,343
We don't want anything bad
to happen to you, Atoy.

327
00:14:04,426 --> 00:14:05,678
We love you.

328
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:07,888
I know.

329
00:14:08,889 --> 00:14:12,810
That's why I know I made
the right decision to retire already.

330
00:14:14,395 --> 00:14:16,188
Then why do you seem

331
00:14:16,272 --> 00:14:17,731
doubtful of your decision?

332
00:14:18,983 --> 00:14:19,942
Huh, Atoy?

333
00:14:20,568 --> 00:14:22,278
Are you still looking for a sign?

334
00:14:23,988 --> 00:14:25,406
Anyway, I'll go ahead.

335
00:14:25,489 --> 00:14:27,241
Emerson asked me to do something.

336
00:14:27,324 --> 00:14:28,951
- Okay.
- Don't disappear.

337
00:14:29,034 --> 00:14:31,203
Emerson's new business
will have its blessing.

338
00:14:31,287 --> 00:14:32,580
You should be there.

339
00:14:32,663 --> 00:14:33,956
- I will be there. I'll make sure.
- He'll feel bad if you're not there.

340
00:14:34,039 --> 00:14:36,333
- Well, all right. I'll go ahead.
- Okay, okay.

341
00:14:36,417 --> 00:14:37,877
[phone vibrating]

342
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:40,379
[gentle music playing]

343
00:14:42,548 --> 00:14:44,717
[sentimental music playing]

344
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:48,220
[Julie] <i>Son, when I'm gone…</i>

345
00:14:48,304 --> 00:14:52,641
[gasps] <i>I'll become a butterfly like this.</i>

346
00:14:53,309 --> 00:14:54,476
<i>So, when…</i>

347
00:14:55,102 --> 00:15:00,190
[sobs] When you're sad or doubtful…

348
00:15:00,274 --> 00:15:01,650
[sobbing]

349
00:15:02,693 --> 00:15:04,069
…I'll show up.

350
00:15:04,945 --> 00:15:05,779
Hmm?

351
00:15:05,863 --> 00:15:08,032
So you'll know

352
00:15:08,115 --> 00:15:10,868
everything will be fine.

353
00:15:21,462 --> 00:15:22,838
[music fades]

354
00:15:22,922 --> 00:15:25,174
Child, why did you bring me here?

355
00:15:25,883 --> 00:15:27,426
Um… What's this?

356
00:15:28,510 --> 00:15:30,846
Actually, this is Daddy's.

357
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:34,850
And these are the disguises and costumes
he used for his missions.

358
00:15:36,769 --> 00:15:38,979
[sighs] Where's your daddy?

359
00:15:40,147 --> 00:15:42,274
- Um…
- I woke up, and he wasn't there.

360
00:15:42,358 --> 00:15:44,568
[gentle music playing]

361
00:15:44,652 --> 00:15:45,611
Oh, what's this?

362
00:15:46,236 --> 00:15:47,446
[Ame] What's this? A garage sale?

363
00:15:48,197 --> 00:15:49,114
[Audrey] Hi!

364
00:15:51,575 --> 00:15:53,369
[Atoy sings] ♪ <i>Oh, Mister Tailor…</i> ♪

365
00:15:55,162 --> 00:15:57,039
[Atoy] Oh?

366
00:16:00,751 --> 00:16:04,129
Ah, love, all these things here…

367
00:16:04,213 --> 00:16:06,131
They all came from the secret room.

368
00:16:07,591 --> 00:16:09,343
Proof that I'm not hiding
anything from you.

369
00:16:10,803 --> 00:16:14,014
[Audrey clicks tongue]

370
00:16:14,098 --> 00:16:17,101
So, I hope you'll give me a chance.

371
00:16:21,063 --> 00:16:22,731
There, oh!

372
00:16:22,815 --> 00:16:23,649
[exclaims and giggles]

373
00:16:23,732 --> 00:16:25,567
Not just Master Cutter,

374
00:16:25,651 --> 00:16:27,111
a romantic magician too.

375
00:16:27,194 --> 00:16:29,029
[in English] Master Atoy.

376
00:16:29,113 --> 00:16:30,072
[Karla teasing]

377
00:16:30,155 --> 00:16:31,532
So, I hope you'll give me a chance, love.

378
00:16:33,075 --> 00:16:34,910
[gentle music playing]

379
00:16:34,994 --> 00:16:35,828
[in English] I love you…

380
00:16:37,579 --> 00:16:38,956
and I'm sorry.

381
00:16:40,207 --> 00:16:41,834
Sorry, because

382
00:16:41,917 --> 00:16:43,627
we argued yesterday.

383
00:16:44,795 --> 00:16:48,716
[clicks tongue] Sorry,
because I had second thoughts

384
00:16:48,799 --> 00:16:50,342
and hesitated giving all this up.

385
00:16:52,386 --> 00:16:55,931
You know, nothing is more important
to me than our family and us.

386
00:16:57,141 --> 00:17:00,019
That's why I brought all these out.

387
00:17:00,102 --> 00:17:02,604
Tomorrow, I'll tear down that secret room.

388
00:17:02,688 --> 00:17:04,023
- [Ame] Oh, you're retiring
- Really?

389
00:17:04,106 --> 00:17:06,191
from being a tracker, Atoy?

390
00:17:06,275 --> 00:17:08,277
But of course, I'll still
be a tailor by day,

391
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:11,363
but a father and husband for life.

392
00:17:11,447 --> 00:17:12,698
That's it!

393
00:17:21,248 --> 00:17:22,332
- Can you?
- Yes!

394
00:17:23,292 --> 00:17:24,585
[huffs]

395
00:17:25,544 --> 00:17:26,879
Whose things are these?

396
00:17:26,962 --> 00:17:28,047
Brother Atoy's too?

397
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:29,048
No.

398
00:17:30,007 --> 00:17:31,216
Mine and Mom's.

399
00:17:32,176 --> 00:17:33,093
[in English] Surprise!

400
00:17:33,177 --> 00:17:34,845
[Karla] We'll live here too for now.

401
00:17:34,928 --> 00:17:36,847
- Really?
- Yes.

402
00:17:37,681 --> 00:17:39,475
Big Brother Atoy himself said so.

403
00:17:39,558 --> 00:17:42,352
Mom and I are renting out
our house for now,

404
00:17:42,436 --> 00:17:46,815
and the two rooms in Big Brother Atoy's
old house are being fixed.

405
00:17:46,899 --> 00:17:50,069
So, while they're being fixed,
we'll stay here.

406
00:17:50,694 --> 00:17:52,029
Isn't it fun?

407
00:17:52,112 --> 00:17:53,155
It's fun indeed.

408
00:17:54,823 --> 00:17:57,117
Now I can be with you anytime I want.

409
00:17:58,035 --> 00:18:01,038
Oh, it's like we're playing house?

410
00:18:01,121 --> 00:18:02,539
[Cita] Hey, hey, hey.

411
00:18:02,623 --> 00:18:05,375
- What do you mean "playing house"?
- Mom, of course--

412
00:18:05,459 --> 00:18:07,211
That's not going to happen
while I'm still alive.

413
00:18:07,294 --> 00:18:08,712
Of course, it was just a joke.

414
00:18:09,588 --> 00:18:11,423
You're so over the top. I was joking.

415
00:18:11,507 --> 00:18:14,551
I don't like that kind of joke,
Karla, Gavin.

416
00:18:14,635 --> 00:18:17,679
I know you have a mutual understanding.

417
00:18:17,763 --> 00:18:19,556
But you should be more careful

418
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:21,892
because you're in the same house.

419
00:18:21,975 --> 00:18:24,144
[Cita] Respect your Brother Atoy's house.

420
00:18:24,812 --> 00:18:26,814
[in English] I understand
your concern, Miss Cita.

421
00:18:27,606 --> 00:18:29,650
I won't do anything you wouldn't like.

422
00:18:29,733 --> 00:18:32,861
[light pleasant music playing]

423
00:18:32,945 --> 00:18:35,447
I need to be sure.

424
00:18:35,531 --> 00:18:36,782
Huh?

425
00:18:44,039 --> 00:18:45,040
[in English] Love…

426
00:18:45,124 --> 00:18:46,542
DELFIN'S TAILORING SHOP

427
00:18:46,625 --> 00:18:49,503
Thank you, because

428
00:18:50,462 --> 00:18:53,257
you chose us over your other job.

429
00:18:53,340 --> 00:18:55,050
[in English] Thank you so much.

430
00:18:56,176 --> 00:18:57,052
It's nothing.

431
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:00,681
You know, this has always been my dream.

432
00:19:01,807 --> 00:19:03,350
Right? To have our family complete.

433
00:19:06,145 --> 00:19:08,355
[gentle music playing]

434
00:19:13,944 --> 00:19:15,279
So, how?

435
00:19:15,362 --> 00:19:19,575
Have you told your boss you're retiring?

436
00:19:21,577 --> 00:19:22,578
[clicks tongue] Not yet.

437
00:19:24,163 --> 00:19:26,415
- [hooter honks]
- He's actually expecting me

438
00:19:26,498 --> 00:19:28,458
to be active again
by the end of the month.

439
00:19:30,377 --> 00:19:32,004
That's why I haven't
spoken to him yet and… [clicks tongue]

440
00:19:32,796 --> 00:19:34,631
I want to talk to him in person.

441
00:19:35,716 --> 00:19:37,009
I want to explain it to him.

442
00:19:38,260 --> 00:19:40,179
I'm sure he'll understand you.

443
00:19:41,305 --> 00:19:44,391
He knows your family is your priority now.

444
00:19:45,767 --> 00:19:47,728
And you've been through so much,

445
00:19:47,811 --> 00:19:50,022
especially during your last mission.

446
00:19:50,647 --> 00:19:52,816
You went up against a big target, Atoy.

447
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:55,319
[tense music playing]

448
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:03,535
[gunshots blasting]

449
00:20:03,619 --> 00:20:05,120
Where is he now?

450
00:20:06,663 --> 00:20:08,749
Any news about Samir?

451
00:20:11,251 --> 00:20:13,420
After he escaped from the hospital,

452
00:20:13,503 --> 00:20:15,297
they say he already left the country.

453
00:20:15,380 --> 00:20:18,926
[inhales] Looks like he won't
be able to come back so easily,

454
00:20:19,009 --> 00:20:20,844
since there's a red notice on him.

455
00:20:24,765 --> 00:20:25,766
[sighs]

456
00:20:29,978 --> 00:20:31,897
[music fades]

457
00:20:31,980 --> 00:20:35,400
LOR 277

458
00:20:35,484 --> 00:20:36,818
MR. FRANK COHEN

459
00:20:37,486 --> 00:20:39,196
[in English] Mr. Frank Cohen!

460
00:20:39,279 --> 00:20:41,073
[in English] Welcome to the Philippines!

461
00:20:41,156 --> 00:20:42,950
[in English] How was your flight?

462
00:20:43,033 --> 00:20:44,993
[in English] Very uncomfortable.

463
00:20:45,077 --> 00:20:46,578
[in English] Oh, I thought
you were an American.

464
00:20:46,662 --> 00:20:48,247
[in English] You don't sound
like an American.

465
00:20:48,997 --> 00:20:49,998
- [Samir] Take this.
- [phone ringing]

466
00:20:50,082 --> 00:20:52,084
[in English] Excuse me for a minute.

467
00:20:52,167 --> 00:20:53,460
[phone vibrating and ringing]

468
00:20:54,962 --> 00:20:55,963
[Artem on the phone] <i>Hello?</i>

469
00:20:56,046 --> 00:20:57,756
[Artem speaking in Russian]

470
00:20:57,839 --> 00:20:59,049
[in English] Hello, Artem.

471
00:21:00,676 --> 00:21:03,011
[in Russian] I have returned to Manila.

472
00:21:03,929 --> 00:21:07,933
[tense music playing]

473
00:21:08,016 --> 00:21:10,602
You're not allowed to stay
in the same room.

474
00:21:11,353 --> 00:21:12,354
[Cita] If it can't be avoided,

475
00:21:12,437 --> 00:21:14,273
the door must not be closed.

476
00:21:14,356 --> 00:21:17,526
You're not allowed to take turns
using the bathroom.

477
00:21:19,111 --> 00:21:20,737
You have to maintain this distance.

478
00:21:20,821 --> 00:21:22,823
You cannot get close to each other.

479
00:21:23,824 --> 00:21:25,993
Mom, that's too much, Mom.

480
00:21:26,076 --> 00:21:28,829
Those are the rules,
so just follow them, okay.

481
00:21:29,454 --> 00:21:31,039
And besides, Atoy already approved it,

482
00:21:31,123 --> 00:21:32,291
even if he doesn't know yet.

483
00:21:33,458 --> 00:21:34,668
Yes, Miss Cita.

484
00:21:34,751 --> 00:21:35,919
No problem with me.

485
00:21:36,003 --> 00:21:40,299
It's fine, but the distance
is no longer correct.

486
00:21:40,382 --> 00:21:42,384
You're already too close to each other.

487
00:21:43,010 --> 00:21:45,304
- [Cita] Stay right there.
- Okay.

488
00:21:45,387 --> 00:21:48,307
[sneaky music playing]

489
00:21:52,269 --> 00:21:53,103
[Atoy] Oh, fine, fine.

490
00:21:53,186 --> 00:21:54,146
Okay. There, there, there.

491
00:21:54,229 --> 00:21:55,314
Oh, everybody! Okay. Here.

492
00:21:55,397 --> 00:21:57,065
Children of the Thread, go!

493
00:21:57,149 --> 00:22:00,944
[Karla] Children of the Thread!

494
00:22:01,028 --> 00:22:03,363
- [cheering]
- Wow!

495
00:22:03,447 --> 00:22:04,906
Come on, let's go inside.

496
00:22:04,990 --> 00:22:06,575
Brothers Kurt and Emerson are there.

497
00:22:06,658 --> 00:22:07,826
- [Karla] Let's go.
- Okay, okay.

498
00:22:07,909 --> 00:22:09,161
- There they are.
- That's fine, Atoy.

499
00:22:09,244 --> 00:22:11,913
So? Is Emerson's surprise okay?

500
00:22:11,997 --> 00:22:14,499
- Huh? [scoffs]
- [overlapping chatter]

501
00:22:14,583 --> 00:22:15,417
[relieved sigh]

502
00:22:16,043 --> 00:22:17,210
I'm really impressed with Emerson.

503
00:22:17,294 --> 00:22:21,048
He really made
Children of the Thread into a business.

504
00:22:21,131 --> 00:22:21,965
- Hey.
- He did continue it.

505
00:22:22,049 --> 00:22:24,009
Amazing. Perfect timing.
I'm retiring soon.

506
00:22:24,092 --> 00:22:26,178
Hey, Atoy, refer us, okay.

507
00:22:26,261 --> 00:22:28,722
If someone's missing
a person, thing, animal,

508
00:22:28,805 --> 00:22:31,058
or losing themselves,

509
00:22:31,141 --> 00:22:32,476
just send them to our office.

510
00:22:32,559 --> 00:22:33,810
We'll take care of it! Okay?

511
00:22:33,894 --> 00:22:35,437
[chuckles] Even that? Of course.

512
00:22:35,520 --> 00:22:36,938
- I'll take care of it. I'll refer you.
- Okay, okay.

513
00:22:37,022 --> 00:22:38,315
[sneaky music playing]

514
00:22:38,398 --> 00:22:40,400
[Paldo] Let's go, let's go.

515
00:22:40,484 --> 00:22:42,402
FATHERS' LANE

516
00:22:43,028 --> 00:22:44,196
Oh, ma'am!

517
00:22:44,279 --> 00:22:47,115
Sorry, I just came from

518
00:22:47,199 --> 00:22:49,367
the opening of my friend's business.

519
00:22:49,451 --> 00:22:52,454
Ah, sorry. Uh… Good, uh… afternoon.

520
00:22:53,914 --> 00:22:55,707
[in English] Anthony Padua, is that you?

521
00:22:57,375 --> 00:22:59,753
Yes. Yes, ma'am. Uh, that's me.

522
00:23:01,004 --> 00:23:02,464
Oh my, sir, it's really you!

523
00:23:02,547 --> 00:23:04,883
I'm Jesabel Marie Garcia,

524
00:23:04,966 --> 00:23:07,469
executive secretary of Sir Mercado.

525
00:23:07,552 --> 00:23:08,595
[quirky sting]

526
00:23:08,678 --> 00:23:10,097
Sir, it's me.

527
00:23:10,180 --> 00:23:11,807
Surprised, sir? I'm beautiful, right?

528
00:23:11,890 --> 00:23:13,767
My little trick, pretending

529
00:23:13,850 --> 00:23:15,894
to be a mysterious girl.

530
00:23:15,977 --> 00:23:17,479
Pretending to be the lady in red.

531
00:23:17,562 --> 00:23:18,563
But the truth is,

532
00:23:18,647 --> 00:23:21,650
I'm just a simple working girl, sir.

533
00:23:21,733 --> 00:23:24,820
Because I'm actually here
to give you your new mission.

534
00:23:25,445 --> 00:23:26,696
Yes. You have a new mission.

535
00:23:26,780 --> 00:23:28,490
Here's your new mission.

536
00:23:28,573 --> 00:23:30,325
Here.

537
00:23:30,408 --> 00:23:31,785
Please open it.

538
00:23:31,868 --> 00:23:33,120
- [in English] Mission?
- [in English] Yes.

539
00:23:33,203 --> 00:23:35,789
I personally delivered it to you.

540
00:23:35,872 --> 00:23:36,706
[Atoy titters]

541
00:23:36,790 --> 00:23:39,084
Oh no, ma'am. I'll just talk to…

542
00:23:39,167 --> 00:23:40,627
Sir Mercado instead.

543
00:23:40,710 --> 00:23:42,504
Oh no. Just open it first.

544
00:23:42,587 --> 00:23:44,631
Look, you'll be surprised. It's beautiful.

545
00:23:44,714 --> 00:23:47,050
[sneaky music playing]

546
00:23:47,134 --> 00:23:48,093
Okay.

547
00:23:51,638 --> 00:23:53,223
CONFIDENTIAL

548
00:23:53,306 --> 00:23:55,976
- [in English] Ta-da! Surprise!
- Oh.

549
00:23:56,059 --> 00:23:57,894
It's me, right?

550
00:23:57,978 --> 00:23:59,521
That means I'm your new mission, sir.

551
00:24:00,313 --> 00:24:01,648
- Yes, me. Mmm-mmm.
- You?

552
00:24:01,731 --> 00:24:02,941
You'll teach me

553
00:24:03,024 --> 00:24:06,153
to become an excellent tracker
in the whole Philippines.

554
00:24:07,112 --> 00:24:08,363
- Ah.
- Mmm-mmm.

555
00:24:08,446 --> 00:24:09,906
Because this is my first…

556
00:24:09,990 --> 00:24:11,366
mentorship program.

557
00:24:11,449 --> 00:24:12,325
[in English] Mentorship program?

558
00:24:12,409 --> 00:24:13,660
I even have a code name.

559
00:24:13,743 --> 00:24:15,579
If you're Master Cutter,

560
00:24:15,662 --> 00:24:16,705
I'm

561
00:24:17,622 --> 00:24:18,874
- The Secretary.
- [quirky sting]

562
00:24:19,457 --> 00:24:21,751
- [in English] Secretary.
- Right? It's like an AI drama.

563
00:24:21,835 --> 00:24:23,461
- [chuckles]
- [in English] Oh, okay.

564
00:24:23,545 --> 00:24:25,463
- That's nice.
- Uh… I told you,

565
00:24:25,547 --> 00:24:27,257
I'll just talk to my boss. So,

566
00:24:27,340 --> 00:24:28,633
- just return it to him when--
- Oh no, sir, because--

567
00:24:28,717 --> 00:24:30,468
Here, here, here. Here.

568
00:24:31,469 --> 00:24:34,055
You'll just talk
at Sir Mercado's birthday celebration.

569
00:24:34,139 --> 00:24:36,141
Because at his 70th birthday,

570
00:24:36,224 --> 00:24:38,476
all the trackers
in the Philippines are invited.

571
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:39,978
For sure, you'll see him there.

572
00:24:40,061 --> 00:24:41,646
You can talk to him there instead

573
00:24:41,730 --> 00:24:43,899
because he told me
he has something to announce.

574
00:24:43,982 --> 00:24:46,109
[in English] A big announcement.

575
00:24:46,193 --> 00:24:48,069
A mission for everyone.

576
00:24:50,405 --> 00:24:51,823
[music fades]

577
00:24:51,907 --> 00:24:53,074
Sir, open it now.

578
00:24:54,284 --> 00:24:56,036
[suspicious music playing]

579
00:24:56,119 --> 00:24:58,371
- [Jesabel] Do you see the red dot, sir?
- [Atoy] Mmm-hmm.

580
00:24:58,455 --> 00:25:03,543
That, sir. Just press that red dot
using your thumb.

581
00:25:03,627 --> 00:25:05,503
- [in English] Thumb.
- [in English] Yes, thumb.

582
00:25:05,587 --> 00:25:08,381
Press it for about five seconds.

583
00:25:08,465 --> 00:25:12,594
Then it will disappear.
[in English] For security purposes.

584
00:25:13,220 --> 00:25:14,221
Press it now.

585
00:25:14,304 --> 00:25:15,889
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

586
00:25:15,972 --> 00:25:20,310
- [in English] One, two, three, four, five.
- [electronic blipping]

587
00:25:21,353 --> 00:25:22,687
[Jesabel] It's gone!

588
00:25:22,771 --> 00:25:23,688
Magic, right?

589
00:25:23,772 --> 00:25:25,357
High-tech. Amazing, right?

590
00:25:25,982 --> 00:25:27,776
But you need to bring it to the optician.

591
00:25:28,860 --> 00:25:29,736
Okay.

592
00:25:29,819 --> 00:25:31,154
[in English] See you, sir.

593
00:25:32,072 --> 00:25:33,031
[in English] Excuse me.

594
00:25:33,949 --> 00:25:35,200
[in English] See you!

595
00:25:38,036 --> 00:25:39,162
[in English] Optician.

596
00:25:41,831 --> 00:25:44,626
I wonder how Mercado
will take my retirement.

597
00:25:46,086 --> 00:25:47,629
Why, love?

598
00:25:47,712 --> 00:25:49,297
Do you think

599
00:25:50,257 --> 00:25:52,008
he won't allow you?

600
00:25:53,134 --> 00:25:55,262
Not really. [sighs]

601
00:25:55,345 --> 00:25:58,640
I'm just sad, because, of course… [sighs]

602
00:25:58,723 --> 00:26:00,475
He's like a father figure to me, right?

603
00:26:01,101 --> 00:26:06,189
He was there for me
when I lost Dad, right?!

604
00:26:06,273 --> 00:26:08,984
- [Audrey sighs]
- And now, I'll tell him I'm retiring,

605
00:26:09,067 --> 00:26:11,194
that I'm leaving, you know.

606
00:26:13,488 --> 00:26:17,617
I think your bond won't disappear

607
00:26:18,326 --> 00:26:19,744
just because you're retired.

608
00:26:21,413 --> 00:26:25,834
A father will always be a father,
no matter what happens.

609
00:26:26,459 --> 00:26:27,460
Right?

610
00:26:30,130 --> 00:26:31,506
[Ibyang] Tatoy, are you ready--

611
00:26:33,383 --> 00:26:34,759
- Hmm?
- [quirky music playing]

612
00:26:34,843 --> 00:26:38,972
Tatoy, that's not the dress code
for our tea party.

613
00:26:39,764 --> 00:26:42,600
Party? Do we-- Do we have--

614
00:26:43,268 --> 00:26:44,352
We have a party today?

615
00:26:45,353 --> 00:26:46,313
You forgot?

616
00:26:47,480 --> 00:26:49,774
Ah, we have a tea party.

617
00:26:50,817 --> 00:26:52,610
Janine is already preparing in the room.

618
00:26:53,361 --> 00:26:56,114
Looks like you double-booked
a party today, love.

619
00:26:56,197 --> 00:26:59,367
[chuckles] Oh, right.

620
00:26:59,451 --> 00:27:01,619
[whimsical music playing]

621
00:27:03,204 --> 00:27:05,206
[in English] He is the last contact
of The Belladonna

622
00:27:05,290 --> 00:27:06,374
before she escaped.

623
00:27:07,292 --> 00:27:10,754
[in English] Levi Mercado, an ex-general
of the local army.

624
00:27:11,921 --> 00:27:13,882
[in English] He leads
an independent tracking

625
00:27:14,924 --> 00:27:17,510
and recovery organization
called The Agency.

626
00:27:18,595 --> 00:27:21,598
[in English] He has trained
a number of man hunters, so…

627
00:27:21,681 --> 00:27:24,642
[clicks tongue] …he must be dangerous.

628
00:27:24,726 --> 00:27:26,686
LAST CONTACT OF THE BELLADONNA…
EX-GENERAL OF THE LOCAL ARMY…

629
00:27:27,354 --> 00:27:30,482
[in English] We must get this man
to extract The Belladonna.

630
00:27:30,565 --> 00:27:33,026
[anticipatory music playing]

631
00:27:33,109 --> 00:27:36,446
[in English] He probably
already knows about the Big Bang plot.

632
00:27:38,448 --> 00:27:40,450
[Artem, in English] Based
on our informant, sir,

633
00:27:41,368 --> 00:27:43,453
this Mercado is organizing an event,

634
00:27:44,496 --> 00:27:46,247
and all the trackers will be there.

635
00:27:48,458 --> 00:27:50,543
[in English] These
are military-trained people.

636
00:27:52,629 --> 00:27:55,548
[in English] Then,
we must be very careful.

637
00:27:56,841 --> 00:27:58,468
[in English] Gather all the information

638
00:27:58,551 --> 00:28:00,053
and we will strike…

639
00:28:03,014 --> 00:28:05,433
and they will never know what hit them.

640
00:28:05,517 --> 00:28:09,312
[music intensifies]

641
00:28:20,573 --> 00:28:23,618
[in English, British accent]
A toast to our father.

642
00:28:23,701 --> 00:28:24,828
Ohh…

643
00:28:24,911 --> 00:28:27,288
[in English, British accent]
To his happy retirement!

644
00:28:27,372 --> 00:28:29,249
- [Ibyang, in English] Yes.
- [British accent] Retirement, indeed.

645
00:28:29,332 --> 00:28:30,166
[chuckles]

646
00:28:30,250 --> 00:28:32,168
- [in English, British accent] That's tea.
- [in English, British accent] Tea.

647
00:28:32,252 --> 00:28:34,921
Samir's group attacked
the event last night.

648
00:28:35,004 --> 00:28:36,381
Big Brother, what's your plan now?

649
00:28:36,464 --> 00:28:38,425
[Karla] <i>Your mortal enemy has returned.</i>

650
00:28:39,050 --> 00:28:39,926
[Samir, in English] Excuse me.

651
00:28:40,009 --> 00:28:42,178
[in English] I am Frank Cohen,

652
00:28:42,262 --> 00:28:43,722
here to meet Danny Guo.

653
00:28:43,805 --> 00:28:44,681
COMING UP

654
00:28:44,764 --> 00:28:46,933
Uh, have you seen this man here?

655
00:28:47,016 --> 00:28:49,102
- [Elias] Uh, I'm a policeman.
- You're a police officer, sir?

656
00:28:49,185 --> 00:28:51,855
[Deiko] <i>Sir, we have a guest here</i>
<i>who is a criminal.</i>

657
00:28:53,273 --> 00:28:54,607
[groans]

658
00:28:54,691 --> 00:28:58,611
[gunshots blasting]

659
00:28:58,695 --> 00:29:00,196
- Take hostages!
- Go!

660
00:29:01,448 --> 00:29:02,615
[Danny] Hurry!

661
00:29:02,699 --> 00:29:04,117
- Come on! [squeals]
- [thumps, then thuds]

662
00:29:04,200 --> 00:29:05,618
[squealing]

663
00:29:06,244 --> 00:29:07,662
[weapon swishes] You're not a woman!

664
00:29:07,746 --> 00:29:09,914
- [swishes]
- [gasps]

665
00:29:13,293 --> 00:29:14,836
THE MASTER CUTTER
CHILDREN OF THE THREAD

666
00:29:14,919 --> 00:29:16,045
♪ <i>Fix this</i> ♪
